{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).$" :multistep/id #uuid "7dd8e6b9-658e-5843-b81d-e4682e166384" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583631}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583669 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583635}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583674 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583583}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583675 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583617}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583689 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583642}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583691 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583596}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583696 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583604}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583712 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186583590}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585025 :multistep/context "![](images/f7/f75f7bf18d9a8fc349dd945227c7e2084b0587552b14a16ab6d73908e296c7bc.png)\n\nThe financial director of a company found that the value of the company's profit $y,$ in thousands of dollars, can be modeled as the union of three curves corresponding to the functions $f(x)$, $g(x),$ and $h(x),$ where $x$ is the number of months since he started keeping track of the profit. The graph is shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "5b2b249c-f012-571e-8cb1-6a0df22d3ab4" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585122 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585100}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585125 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585043}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585130 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585053}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585132 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585088}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585168 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585030}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585169 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585093}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585175 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585049}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585176 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585059}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585713 :multistep/context "Consider the functions $f(x)=2{x}^{A}-B,g(x)=A{e}^{x},$ and $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1,$ where $A$ and $B$ are constants to be found." :multistep/id #uuid "65636e3c-ba71-595d-8fca-e2e645b391f9" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585818 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585745}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585831 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585809}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585837 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585731}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585838 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585772}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585840 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585738}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585855 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585744}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585856 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585727}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585864 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585714}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587277 :multistep/context "![](images/8a/8a7ce3e8e48aef09686ae60c7f7194e064538be34aa0faa183d9a5fe74352fa2.png)\n\nAn economist monitoring a certain currency found that the inflation $y,$ in $\\%,$ can be modeled as the union of three curves corresponding to the functions $f(x)$, $g(x),$ and $h(x),$ where $x$ is the number of months since he started keeping track of the inflation. The graph is shown above." :multistep/id #uuid "31953a4d-8b63-5884-859a-04294945586b" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587383 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587304}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587354}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587412 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587308}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587419 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587346}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587440 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587310}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587441 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587363}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587442 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587376}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587446 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186587330}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594664 :multistep/context "A particle $P$ is moving along a curve in an $xy$-plane such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+3)^{2}},\\,t>0\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is the distance of $P$ from the origin, measured in meters, and $t$ is measured in seconds." :multistep/id #uuid "cda1fd0e-ac68-5a35-9383-0f5598e0801a" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594743 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594665}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594754 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594680}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594756 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594693}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594761 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594720}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594763 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594682}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594780 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594728}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594782 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594697}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594783 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594705}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594722}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594799 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594690}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596619 :multistep/context "![](images/d0/d0e8cc7d5f289d2bfaa33a21347b4ee60c1e89b58eb0076003d5f37c2ab9e1a8.png)\n\nConsider a continuous function $f$ defined on the closed interval $-8\\le x\\le 5.$ The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above for the region $-5\\le x\\le 5,$ and consists of two line segments and an arc of a quarter circle centered at $(0,0)$ with radius $2.$ It is known that the point $(-1,-\\sqrt{3})$ is on the graph of $f.$" :multistep/id #uuid "6c635149-ee4a-5f11-84e7-a597b9024876" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596725 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596672}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596732 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596667}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596737 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596673}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596743 